<section class="section pricing-explanation" aria-labelledby="price-differences-heading">
  <div class="container">
    <div class="pricing-intro prose">
      <h2 id="price-differences-heading">Why these prices differ</h2>
      <p>The examples cover different amounts of design and production work. Here is what to consider when comparing them with your own project.</p>
    </div>
    <div class="pricing-factor-grid">
      <div class="prose">
        <h3>Design work</h3>
        <p>The <a href="#price-radio">radio cover</a> was recreated from a damaged original; the <a href="#price-rack">rack adapters</a> were designed for specific equipment. Send an existing model if you have one, or tell us what needs to be designed.</p>
      </div>
      <div class="prose">
        <h3>Quantity</h3>
        <p>The <a href="#price-scrapers">£0.75 scraper price</a> applied to a batch of 220. CAD was included in the <a href="#price-bobbins">resin bobbin prices</a> for orders of several parts. Neither is a price for a new one-off design.</p>
      </div>
      <div class="prose">
        <h3>Geometry, material and process</h3>
        <p>A large radio grille and small resin bobbins need different printing methods and preparation. Size alone does not determine the price: detail, supports, fit and material also matter. <a href="{{ '/materials/' | url }}">Explore materials</a>.</p>
      </div>
      <div class="prose">
        <h3>Finishing and delivery</h3>
        <p>The scraper batch included individual packaging and stickers. Other work may need different finishing or packing. Delivery is shown separately in the examples; your quote will set out the work and delivery agreed for your order.</p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

